* Course 07 final exam -- the microsecond-scale transients (Questions 4 and 13c) confirmed in ngspice.
* Q4: a 10 V step into a series RLC at rest (step at t = 0 with a 1 ns ramp; the half-nanosecond offset is
*     negligible at these tolerances).
* Q13c: the buck converter's output filter with the switch node held at its 3 V average and a 1 ohm load;
*     a 2 A current sink steps on at t = 10 us (the exam's t = 0). ESR is ignored, as in the question.
*
* EXPECT q4i   key:solutions.md#X07.4i rtol=1e-4
* EXPECT q4j   key:solutions.md#X07.4j scale=1e-6 rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT q13k  key:solutions.md#X07.13k rtol=1e-3
* EXPECT q13j  key:solutions.md#X07.13j scale=1e-6 rtol=2e-3

* ---- Q4
V4   s4 0 PWL(0 0 1n 10)
R4   s4 x4 20
L4   x4 y4 1m
VI4  y4 c4 DC 0
C4   c4 0 1u
* ---- Q13c
V13  sw 0 DC 3
L13  sw o 2.2u
C13  o 0 47u
R13  o 0 1
I13  o 0 PWL(0 0 10u 0 10.001u 2)

.options reltol=1e-7 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-10
.control
tran 2n 200u 0 2n
meas tran q4i max v(c4) from=0 to=200u
meas tran tvp max_at v(c4) from=0 to=200u
meas tran q4l max i(VI4) from=0 to=100u
meas tran tip max_at i(VI4) from=0 to=100u
let q4j = tvp - 0.5n
let q4k = tip - 0.5n
print q4j q4k
meas tran vmin min v(o) from=10u to=60u
meas tran tmin min_at v(o) from=10u to=60u
let q13k = 3 - vmin
let q13j = tmin - 10.0005u
print q13k q13j
.endc
.end
